Active Orchestration & Pipeline Flow: Shift from passive processing to active orchestration by overlapping tasks. During mandatory cooking durations, never idle or remain stationary. Proactively transition to the next resource source (e.g., securing a serving dish or repositioning to the onion dispenser) to ensure continuous workflow. Maintain a single-item inventory loop but maximize throughput by staging the next ingredient immediately after starting a cook cycle.

